<title>UK: UK Allied Domecq buys U.S. sandwich chain.</title>
<headline>UK Allied Domecq buys U.S. sandwich chain.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>British drinks group Allied Domecq said on Monday its retailing unit had bought Togo's, a U.S. sandwich store chain for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>The company said the California-based, 200-store chain had assets valued at five million stg.</p>
<p>Allied said the consideration was not material in relation to its net assets.</p>
<p>Togo's will be managed along with Allied Domecq Retailing's existing food service brands, Dunkin Donuts and Baskin-Robbins.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
